# Line endings are declared here rather than left to core.autocrlf, which is a property
# of a machine and not of this repository. Without this file the two disagree silently:
# git diff compares normalized content, so a working tree holding a mix of CRLF and LF
# reports clean, while anything that compares raw bytes -- a generated table, a golden
# file, a digest of a source tree -- fails against it with no visible cause. This
# repository derives identity from bytes, so it is more exposed to that than most.

# Normalize every text file in the index to LF, and check it out as LF everywhere.
# `text=auto eol=lf` rather than plain `text=auto` so a Windows checkout is the same
# bytes as a Linux one, which is what makes the gate's ubuntu runner and a developer's
# machine able to agree about a file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts that genuinely require CRLF, listed even though none exist yet,
# because the next person to add one should find the seam rather than invent it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git never rewrites a byte of it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
